text:
It was too late to call it a day,

But I saw my life as one long dream,

And so I woke up and took another way;

And I was afraid to go, and came down by that river-side,
The wind was very high
As we sailed along there came up the sun

Though it has not been spoken since then, yet his voice is still heard;
And now she’s gone, too far away for me to hear him speak;

The child and the teacher, they stand together now;
 They see themselves in each other's face so true;
 The girl with the golden hair, that was so shy then,
 Now is one who sees herself and all she can be.
